<!-- Main.storyboard placeholder

This file describes the structure of the main storyboard for xLights.
The actual .storyboard file should be created in Xcode's Interface Builder.

When creating the storyboard in Xcode:

1. Create new Storyboard file named "Main.storyboard"
2. Add the following scenes:

Scene 1: Main Window Controller
- Identifier: "MainWindowController"
- Class: NSWindowController (will be replaced with custom class in 1A)
- Window size: 1200x800
- Window style: Titled, Closable, Miniaturizable, Resizable
- Content view controller: MainViewController

Scene 2: Main View Controller
- Identifier: "MainViewController"
- Class: NSViewController (will be replaced with custom class in 1A)
- View layout:
  - Top: NSToolbar (play controls, tool mode selectors)
  - Body: NSSplitView (three regions - will be implemented in 1A)
    - Left: Setup/Layout/Sequencer tabs
    - Center: Preview/Timeline
    - Right: Inspector sidebar
  - Bottom: Status bar (optional)

Storyboard Structure:
```
MainWindowController
  └─ MainViewController
      └─ NSSplitView
          ├─ LeftViewController (Setup tab)
          ├─ CenterViewController (Preview/Timeline)
          └─ RightViewController (Inspector)
```

Document Architecture Setup:
- NSDocumentController: XLDocumentController
- NSDocument: XLDocument
- Initial Scene: MainWindowController

Storyboard Segues:
- None (document-based app, not navigation-based)

Toolbar Items (to be added in Phase 1B):
- Play/Pause/Stop buttons
- Timeline position slider
- View toggles (inspector, timeline, waveform)
- Zoom controls

This placeholder file should be replaced with an actual .storyboard file
created in Xcode Interface Builder during Phase 1A integration.

Alternative: Skip storyboard and create window/views programmatically
in NSWindowController subclass (recommended for complex layouts).
-->
